      "background_kind": "curated",
      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Z buffer.svg",
      "heading": "Painted order or **tested** depth?",
      "sentence": "A 2.5-D web layer is sorted **back to front** once. A 3-D engine stores a depth value for every pixel and tests it **every frame**, so crossing shapes stay honest.",
      "prompt": "Photogrammetry goes further and **measures** depth from many photos — but shiny, black or sheer cloth often scans badly.",
      "image_brief": "A Z-buffer diagram: a simple 3D scene beside its depth image, nearer surfaces brighter.",
      "notes": "- 2.5-D parallax on a portfolio site is painter's order, not 3-D.\n- Marr's 2½-D sketch: depth per point, seen from one place.",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-VD-C.masterclass-depth-test"
    },
